{
  "note": [
    "Which of Jack Antonoff and Aaron Dessner is credited as a producer on a song, and the",
    "full producer line it is read off. `by` is one of \"jack\", \"aaron\" or \"both\", and it",
    "answers ONLY that question: it says nothing about whether Taylor, Max Martin or anyone",
    "else is on the record too. \"jack\" means Antonoff is credited and Dessner is not.",
    "",
    "A song absent from this file has NEITHER of them on it. That is how a title opts out —",
    "there is no fourth bucket, and The Life of a Showgirl is absent entirely for that reason",
    "rather than by an oversight (Swift, Max Martin and Shellback produced it).",
    "",
    "`credit` is the real producer line and exists to be PRINTED at a reveal, not to be parsed.",
    "Do not derive `by` from it: a vocal-production or additional-production credit names people",
    "who do not change the bucket, which is why \"Nothing New\" is aaron with Tony Berg on the",
    "line and \"Fortnight\" is jack with Louis Bell on it.",
    "",
    "Four rulings this file bakes in, so they are not re-litigated from the data later:",
    "  1. folklore is read off the JULY 2020 RELEASE CREDITS, not later database metadata",
    "     rewritten around the William Bowery disclosure.",
    "  2. A Taylor's Version re-recording is NOT a second entry. The four that would collapse",
    "     (Out of the Woods, I Wish You Would, You Are in Love, Sweeter than Fiction) carry the",
    "     same producer as their originals, so the original's row stands for both.",
    "  3. Remixes, acoustic cuts, piano versions and long pond performances are not songs here.",
    "     All Too Well (10 Minute Version) IS, because it is its own studio master.",
    "  4. Songs released under another artist's name are out — Big Red Machine's Renegade and",
    "     Birch, the National's The Alcott, and Gracie Abrams's us., which would otherwise be a",
    "     fifth \"both\".",
    "",
    "Album and track order mirror data/songs.json exactly, so the two files diff against each",
    "other. Every title here is spelled as songs.json spells it and matches it on a straight",
    "lookup — no normalising needed at the call site."
  ],
